                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8b18451c-a4ea-3316-8867-a190b44106c6",
                        "entry_id": "1ee920d9-2d20-3b9b-9e2f-4f59939016db",
                        "glosses": [
                            "муз. струнно-щипковый музыкальный инструмент, род гитары с резонатором"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ccfcb81-1fa5-47b3-8d86-38361ec9e4d3",
                                "sense_id": "8b18451c-a4ea-3316-8867-a190b44106c6",
                                "text": "В студии многие удивились, когда на вопрос, кто на чём хочет учиться играть, я выкрикнул: «На банджо!» Большинство, естественно, хотели научиться играть на трубе, аккордеоне, саксофоне… А я ― на банджо. Желание играть на этом инструменте возникло после просмотра английского фильма «Джордж из Динки-джаза», герой которого пел песни, аккомпанируя себе на банджо."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "691f2435-ffc2-49d3-998a-5b93ea64004e",
                        "source_entry_id": "1ee920d9-2d20-3b9b-9e2f-4f59939016db",
                        "source_sense_id": "8b18451c-a4ea-3316-8867-a190b44106c6",
                        "target_lang_word": "banjo",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "banjo",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3a66a35-fc39-3b29-ac7f-e5ded459489f",
                                        "entry_id": "b1adad69-05a9-3f16-b5a4-04e17f2c1108",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A stringed musical instrument (chordophone), usually with a round body, a membrane-like soundboard and a fretted neck, played by plucking or strumming the strings."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29700eb7-23ac-4a99-bdb8-a39b2ece9cd2",
                                                "sense_id": "a3a66a35-fc39-3b29-ac7f-e5ded459489f",
                                                "text": "I come from Alabama with my banjo on my knee..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "418a7cc8-71e2-462a-b0c8-1fe59c2b5707",
                                                "sense_id": "a3a66a35-fc39-3b29-ac7f-e5ded459489f",
                                                "text": "For quotations using this term, see Citations:banjo."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "631e29f8-288b-32ce-8027-6598c7edb89f",
                                        "entry_id": "b1adad69-05a9-3f16-b5a4-04e17f2c1108",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of various similar musical instruments, such as the Tuvan doshpuluur, with a membrane-like soundboard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "690c5759-ca7f-3efd-8391-cfa2cddd8019",
                                        "entry_id": "b1adad69-05a9-3f16-b5a4-04e17f2c1108",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An object shaped like a banjo, especially a frying pan or a shovel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28ed047c-daf0-330a-98d2-4e78f934455e",
                                        "entry_id": "b1adad69-05a9-3f16-b5a4-04e17f2c1108",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A cul-de-sac with a round end."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "054547ad-4e55-4fab-82ad-b0bedf56b6d3",
                                                "sense_id": "28ed047c-daf0-330a-98d2-4e78f934455e",
                                                "text": "Billy Tower lived in the far left house in the banjo that was Dagenham's version of cul de sacs. The trouble was you could be seen from the house and, in the time it took to walk along the Banjo, drugs could be flushed away."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77b75ced-61fd-47d1-b867-cc8b675b4462",
                                                "sense_id": "28ed047c-daf0-330a-98d2-4e78f934455e",
                                                "text": "They all came back here — we cleared the room and put up tables for the reception — and then we went to another house on the banjo for a \"knees-up\"."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b59afd6-0793-4f2d-85a2-97c2fcaeb028",
                                                "sense_id": "28ed047c-daf0-330a-98d2-4e78f934455e",
                                                "text": "The banjo format is not an unalloyed success these days: kids playing noisily on the quite narrow common green […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e3f45999-5c30-3f71-a224-f355ac1754cc",
                                        "entry_id": "b1adad69-05a9-3f16-b5a4-04e17f2c1108",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A miner's round-nosed shovel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "70b97892-4da2-316f-bcc4-25204f18ce22",
                                        "entry_id": "b1adad69-05a9-3f16-b5a4-04e17f2c1108",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An egg sandwich fried on a flattop and served in a bun as would a burger, ellipsis of egg banjo."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Malaysia"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "621f575e-03da-39a8-bfdb-6ab3b2c49abf",
                                        "entry_id": "b1adad69-05a9-3f16-b5a4-04e17f2c1108",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The frenulum of the penis."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "vulgar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "banjo",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b9710412-f971-3aa2-905a-8c98776b541e",
                                        "entry_id": "1de4e392-91d3-398e-acde-c6c3c2f6999d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To play a banjo."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d96e4280-41bf-3a17-9710-a0ab7d807fba",
                                        "entry_id": "1de4e392-91d3-398e-acde-c6c3c2f6999d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To beat, to knock down."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "slang",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a89fbf6-5c95-4371-b534-ec874b5210a0",
                                                "sense_id": "d96e4280-41bf-3a17-9710-a0ab7d807fba",
                                                "text": "Admitting the assault, the husband said that he had given her a 'banjoing' but that she had asked for it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edfc3eb6-5747-4145-a180-e2206a85726d",
                                                "sense_id": "d96e4280-41bf-3a17-9710-a0ab7d807fba",
                                                "text": "Madar was turfed out on a final misdemeanour of banjoing one of his teammates in training before a big game"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36b86212-bd05-497b-b9e9-0ca2c40fa959",
                                                "sense_id": "d96e4280-41bf-3a17-9710-a0ab7d807fba",
                                                "text": "\"Me and other folk were just trying to get the boot in and some other guy banjoed [decked] him”."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "38feef85-0540-32f9-a9a0-1d6fe85e8de8",
                                        "entry_id": "1de4e392-91d3-398e-acde-c6c3c2f6999d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To shell or attack (a target)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "slang",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a278e6d9-46a0-40cb-8dd4-54a8285c7c33",
                                                "sense_id": "38feef85-0540-32f9-a9a0-1d6fe85e8de8",
                                                "text": "Riding reported that on the day Mayne had asked for DZ coordinates, their base had been banjoed by the Germans."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
